    <p>Lightweight and blazing-fast, running sub-second translations on standard laptops without requiring specialized hardware.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 id="architecture">3. Seq2Seq Architecture &amp; How It Works</h2>
<p>Xetu translates between English and Assamese through four synchronized stages:</p>
<ol class="flow">
  <li><strong>Subword Segmentation:</strong> Source text is tokenized against a unified 122,672 vocabulary spanning Latin and Bengali scripts, resolving prefixation and morphological boundaries cleanly.</li>
  <li><strong>Encoder Contextualization:</strong> The multi-layer transformer encoder builds continuous semantic representations of the entire source sentence, preserving thematic dependencies across clause boundaries.</li>
  <li><strong>Autoregressive Decoder with Cross-Attention:</strong> The decoder generates the target translation word-by-word while cross-attending to encoder states, enforcing strict grammatical agreement in noun-verb conjugations.</li>
  <li><strong>4-Beam Search Ranking:</strong> Hypotheses are dynamically ranked using beam search with length penalties, selecting the most fluent, grammatically natural Assamese formulation.</li>
</ol>

