      <details class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><summary itemprop="name">Why is Axom AI Xetu better than Google Translate for Assamese?</summary><div class="faq-body" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><div itemprop="text"><p>Google Translate relies on generic multilingual models that frequently scramble Assamese case endings (-ৰ, -লৈ, -ত) and translate idioms literally. Axom AI Xetu is a specialized 200M Seq2Seq model trained directly on parallel Assam administrative, educational, and cultural data, ensuring grammatical fidelity.</p></div></div></details><details class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><summary itemprop="name">Can Axom AI Xetu be deployed completely offline?</summary><div class="faq-body" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><div itemprop="text"><p>Yes. The entire model fits into 1.03 GB of storage and operates under 850 MB of RAM, allowing government departments, legal chambers, and healthcare providers to run 100% private translations without connecting to the internet.</p></div></div></details><details class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><summary itemprop="name">Does Xetu support technical and legal vocabularies?</summary><div class="faq-body" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><div itemprop="text"><p>Yes. Xetu is explicitly calibrated on Assam state gazettes, legislative bills, land revenue terms, and educational texts, making it highly accurate for technical and administrative documents.</p></div></div></details><details class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><summary itemprop="name">Who owns the rights to Axom AI Xetu?</summary><div class="faq-body" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><div itempr